# Keeps the Docker build context to what a from-source build needs. The
# Dockerfile's `build` stage copies the whole context, so everything listed
# here is either regenerated inside the build, irrelevant to it, or something
# that must never leave this machine.
#
# Docker matches a bare `name/` only at the context root; `**/name` is what
# matches at any depth.

# Regenerated by the build.
**/target
**/node_modules
dist/
data/

# Never in an image. `.env` holds live credentials on a developer machine; the
# example is the only env file a build may see.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not redistributable, and not read by any build step: dev and test fixtures.
example/

# Irrelevant to a build.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.hooks/
specs/
docs/
test-results/
playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/torture-results/
apps/web/e2e/.demo/
